  "verbalization": "Cocosamide B is implicated in the biological pathway leading to SNU-387 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Cocosamide B acts as a target for multiple entities, including MOVP-3, Hepatocyte, and SNB-78, all of which are targets of the same compound, 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One. This compound is consistently identified as a target of Cocosamide B in all three paths, with a high final score in each, indicating a strong and reliable relationship. The shared target of this compound with SNU-387 suggests a potential mechanism of action where the compound modulates the activity of 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, which in turn affects SNU-387. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Cocosamide B in influencing the biological processes of SNU-387 through the indirect action of this intermediate compound.",
